## Current Model Status

**Math models — complete:**
- carrabin: Bayes (optimal), NoisyCounting (human-matching, n_runs=50), RL (naive)
- jiang: Bayes (optimal, soft probabilistic), DeGroot (human-matching), RL (naive)
- yoo: Mean (optimal), ADM (human-matching, nu fixed=0.01), RL (naive)

**NEF models — in development:**
- `models/counting.py` — standalone counting circuit testbed (complete)
- `models/synaptic.py` — full synaptic NEF model (stub)
- `models/recurrent.py` — recurrent NEF model (stub)

**Known model details:**
- NoisyCounting: sigma_c and nu upper bounds widened to 2.0
- ADM: nu fixed at 0.01 per Yoo et al.; only phi and rho are fitted
- Jiang Bayes: soft probabilistic; signal accuracy = 5/7
- Jiang models: continuous expectations saved in response files; beta
  sampling applied post-hoc via `apply_beta_sampling()` in switch_probability_jiang.py

